<%@ include file="header.jsp"%>
<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">
	<h2 class="mb-4">About OpenLibrary</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>OpenLibrary</strong> is a free, open-access document sharing
		platform designed to support students, educators, and independent
		learners in sharing and discovering digital content such as eBooks,
		PDF notes, and study materials. Whether you're looking to contribute
		knowledge or explore resources, OpenLibrary offers a fast,
		user-friendly, and secure environment.
	</p>

	<h4 class="mt-4">Project Overview</h4>
	<p>
		OpenLibrary is developed as a dynamic web application using <strong>Jakarta
			Servlets</strong>, <strong>JSP (JavaServer Pages)</strong>, and <strong>MySQL</strong>
		as the backend database. The project follows a modular MVC
		(Model-View-Controller) architecture for scalability and
		maintainability. It is deployed as a Dynamic Web Project using Eclipse
		IDE and supports UTF-8 encoding to ensure compatibility with global
		character sets.
	</p>

	<h4 class="mt-4">Key Features</h4>
	<ul>
		<li>User registration for uploading documents</li>
		<li>Upload eBooks and notes with title, author, description,
			category, and cover image</li>
		<li>Public document downloads without login</li>
		<li>Search functionality by title, author, or category</li>
		<li>Edit or update uploaded documents</li>
		<li>Clean, responsive interface with header and footer templates</li>
	</ul>

	<h4 class="mt-4">Use Cases</h4>
	<p>OpenLibrary is ideal for:
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Students</strong> sharing class notes or project
			reports</li>
		<li><strong>Teachers</strong> distributing study material or
			assignments</li>
		<li><strong>Developers and writers</strong> sharing technical
			documents or eBooks</li>
		<li><strong>Institutions</strong> creating a digital repository
			of learning materials</li>
	</ul>


	<p>
		OpenLibrary is and always will be <strong>free to use</strong>,
		helping bridge the gap between knowledge providers and seekers. Join
		us in creating an open learning ecosystem.
	</p>

	<p class="text-muted">
		Have questions or suggestions? <a href="contact.jsp">Get in touch</a>
		- we'd love to hear from you.
	</p>
</div>


